# Characters

Draw people so that they explain the task and include every member of a household. civica has no fixed set of characters.

<h2 id="bg-ill-05">Shapes</h2>

Build a person from simple shapes: a round head, a rounded rectangle for the body and curved lines for the arms. Draw believable proportions.

Do not draw eyes, a mouth or other facial features. People then read the scene from body language, not from one expression.

## Representation

Show a range of:

- ages
- skin tones
- body types
- clothing, including religious dress
- disabilities, such as a person using a wheelchair or a walking stick

Do not assume who owns the home or who does a chore. Do not use a person’s look to suggest their identity or ability.

## Body language

Show people doing something, alone or together, such as 2 people fitting a sensor. A turn of the body or a reaching arm tells the story without a face.

